<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Optus postpones results presentations.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Optus postpones results presentations.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Optus Communications Pty Ltd said on Monday that it had postponed financial results presentations scheduled for Tuesday and Wednesday, citing uncertainty arising from litigation by Seven Network Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Optus Communications postponed the announcement in order to provide shareholders with the opportunity to discuss the half year accounts and the issues related to Optus Vision at its regular meeting, scheduled for February 27,&quot; Optus said.</p>
<p>Optus was scheduled to release half year results on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Seven Network said on Friday that it accepted offers to buy the remaining 98 percent of pay television operator Optus Vision it does not already own.</p>
<p>The two offers made to Seven's subsidiary Tallglen arise from a legal dispute between the television network and the other Optus Vision shareholders.</p>
<p>Seven initiated the legal action, alleging the shareholders had breached the Optus Vision shareholders agreement and claiming that this meant Seven had the right to buyout the majority holdings.</p>
</text>
